---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout
  title="GxP Clinical Data Migration | KSM Technology Partners"
  description="Purpose-built clinical data migration for regulated pharma environments. Audit-ready lineage, access controls, and tooling built for GxP from the ground up."
>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 1: Hero
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Moving content is the easy part.</h1>
    <p>
      In a GxP environment, regulatory requirements run through every decision —
      every transfer, every access control choice, every deviation from the plan.
      Most teams don't underestimate the technical complexity. They underestimate
      what GxP adds to it.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="../contact" class="btn">Schedule a Scoping Workshop</a>
    </div>
    <p class="trust-line">Delivered at multiple top-10 pharma companies.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Stats Bar
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="stats-bar">
    <div class="stats-bar-inner">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-num">10+</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Top-Pharma Engagements</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-num">100s</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Studies Migrated</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-num">0</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Audit Findings</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-num">GxP</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Purpose-Built</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 2: Where GxP Complexity Lives
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Where GxP complexity lives in data migration</h2>
      <div class="grid-2 mt-2">

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with document/mapping icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/><polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Data Mapping</h3>
          <p>Legacy-to-target translation must be solved before you move a single byte — for code, data, and structure.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with shield/audit icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Auditability</h3>
          <p>Can you prove things changed only when and how you said? Transparency is required from start to finish.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with lock icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Access Control</h3>
          <p>Not a post-migration task. Unauthorized access to study data is a regulatory event.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <!-- TODO: Replace with checklist icon -->
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="9 11 12 14 22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Documentation</h3>
          <p>A plan before, a report after, and a deviation record. Every pharma defines their own requirements — does your migration process support them?</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Platform Logos Strip
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="logos-strip">
    <div class="logos-strip-inner">
      <span class="logos-label">Works with the platforms your team already uses</span>
      <div class="logos-row">
        <!-- Domino Data Lab -->
        <div class="logo-item">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 120 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Domino Data Lab">
            <circle cx="10" cy="16" r="5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7"/>
            <circle cx="26" cy="10" r="3.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7"/>
            <circle cx="26" cy="22" r="3.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7"/>
            <text x="38" y="21" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">Domino</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <!-- Terraform -->
        <div class="logo-item">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 110 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Terraform">
            <polygon points="8,6 18,12 18,24 8,18" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.55"/>
            <polygon points="20,0 30,6 30,18 20,12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7"/>
            <polygon points="20,14 30,20 30,32 20,26" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"/>
            <text x="36" y="21" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">Terraform</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <!-- Git -->
        <div class="logo-item">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 80 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Git">
            <rect x="4" y="10" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.7"/>
            <rect x="22" y="4" width="14" height="14" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.7"/>
            <line x1="11" y1="10" x2="29" y2="18" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" opacity="0.5"/>
            <text x="42" y="21" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">Git</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <!-- AWS S3 -->
        <div class="logo-item">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 100 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="AWS S3">
            <path d="M8 22 L16 8 L24 22 Z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.7"/>
            <circle cx="16" cy="22" r="3" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"/>
            <text x="32" y="21" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">AWS / Azure</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <!-- SAS -->
        <div class="logo-item">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 70 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="SAS">
            <path d="M6 20 Q6 10 16 10 Q26 10 16 16 Q6 22 16 22 Q26 22 26 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.7"/>
            <text x="36" y="21" font-family="system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">SAS</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 3: Credibility
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="credibility-layout">
      <img 
        src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/services/cdc_scientist2.jpg`}
        alt="Scientist working in a regulated laboratory environment"
        class="credibility-image"
      />
      <div>
        <blockquote class="pullquote">
          <p>"We've run this at multiple top-10 pharma companies."</p>
          <footer>Data migration in regulated life sciences is a deep practice — not a side capability.</footer>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="prose">
          <blockquote>
            "The technical challenges are solvable. Derailments are almost always in planning, mapping, and governance — not execution."
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 4: Our Approach — Controlled, Not Big Bang
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <h2>Controlled. Not big bang.</h2>
      <p class="intro-para">
        We break the migration into executable, governable units — study-level
        groupings with discrete ownership, independent state, and safe retry.
        Active studies don't get disrupted. Cutover happens in managed waves.
      </p>
      <div class="grid-2 feature-grid">

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Migration Units</h3>
          <p>Study-level or equivalent groupings with clear ownership and status.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Per-Unit State</h3>
          <p>Each unit tracks its own state independently — safely retryable without affecting completed work.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Controlled Cutover</h3>
          <p>Managed transitions in waves, not a single high-risk switchover.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="feature-item">
          <h3>Bounded Scope</h3>
          <p>Clearly defined operational limits at every stage.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 4b: Traditional vs. KSM Comparison
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="overline">Why it matters</span>
      <h2>Most migrations weren't designed for GxP.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="comparison-table">
      <div class="comparison-col comparison-col--old">
        <div class="comparison-col-header">
          <span class="comparison-badge comparison-badge--old">Typical Approach</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="comparison-list">
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--bad">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
            Audit trail assembled after the fact from logs
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--bad">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
            Access controls configured post-migration
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--bad">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
            Big-bang cutover with high rollback risk
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--bad">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
            Generic ETL tools adapted for regulated use
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--bad">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
            Documentation produced manually at close
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--bad">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"/><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"/></svg>
            Failed runs require restarting from scratch
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-col comparison-col--new">
        <div class="comparison-col-header">
          <span class="comparison-badge comparison-badge--new">KSM Approach</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="comparison-list">
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--good">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            Lineage events emitted during execution — not reconstructed
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--good">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            Access controls provisioned as code before cutover
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--good">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            Controlled waves with per-unit state and safe retry
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--good">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            KMT built ground-up for GxP regulated environments
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--good">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            Documentation is a byproduct of execution
          </li>
          <li class="comparison-item comparison-item--good">
            <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            Each unit retries independently — completed work is never re-run
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 5: Purpose-Built Tooling (KMT)
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="tooling-layout">

      <div>
        <h2>Purpose-built tooling for regulated data migration into Domino.</h2>
        <p class="intro-para">
          The KSM Migration Toolkit (KMT) was built specifically for the challenges
          of migrating clinical data into modern platforms like Domino.
          This is not a generic ETL tool adapted for this use case. It was designed for it.
        </p>

        <div class="capability-list">

          <div class="capability-item">
            <h3>Infrastructure-as-code execution</h3>
            <p>Via Terraform — deterministic, repeatable, peer-reviewed before it touches target systems.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="capability-item">
            <h3>Native Domino connector</h3>
            <p>Provisions organizations, projects, volumes, access controls, and syncpoints as code.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="capability-item">
            <h3>Git-managed configuration</h3>
            <p>Every change is traceable, reviewable, and auditable.</p>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="browser-frame">
        <div class="browser-chrome">
          <div class="browser-dots">
            <span></span><span></span><span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="browser-bar">KSM Migration Toolkit — Lineage Graph</div>
        </div>
        <div class="browser-body">
          <img
            src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/services/saga_screenshot_graph.png`}
            alt="Lineage graph showing jobs, datasets, and transfers connected in a navigable audit graph"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="image-caption">Every job. Every dataset. Every transfer. Connected in a navigable, auditable graph — built during the migration, not reconstructed afterward.</figcaption>
      </figure>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 6: Audit Trail
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="audit-card">
        <div class="audit-card-header">
          <span class="overline">For QA &amp; Validation</span>
          <h2>Your QA team gets evidence, not assurances.</h2>
          <p class="intro-para">Documentation as a byproduct of execution — not assembled after the fact.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2 audit-grid">

          <div class="audit-item">
            <div class="card-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Timestamped Events</h3>
              <p>Every step emits a lineage event with a unique run ID — source to staging, staging to target.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-item">
            <div class="card-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Auto-attached Results</h3>
              <p>Validation results, checksums, and row counts automatically attached to the lineage record.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-item">
            <div class="card-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="9 11 12 14 22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Built During Execution</h3>
              <p>A complete audit trail — not reconstructed from logs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="audit-item">
            <div class="card-icon">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Deviation Records</h3>
              <p>When expected outcomes aren't met, it's captured and traceable.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 6b: Who This Is For
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-heading centered text-center">
      <span class="overline">Who we work with</span>
      <h2>Built for the teams who own the risk.</h2>
      <p>Regulatory complexity touches every stakeholder. KMT gives each team what they actually need.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-3 personas-grid">

      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Regulatory Affairs</h3>
        <p>Full audit trail, deviation records, and validation packages produced automatically — not assembled from spreadsheets after the fact.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Data Engineers</h3>
        <p>Infrastructure-as-code via Terraform. Git-managed configuration. Every migration unit is independently retryable without touching completed work.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>IT &amp; Security</h3>
        <p>Access controls provisioned before any data moves. Every permission is reviewable, peer-approved, and traceable to a Git commit.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="9 11 12 14 22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Validation Teams</h3>
        <p>Checksums, row counts, and validation results auto-attached to every lineage record. Your IQ/OQ documentation is built during execution.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"/><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"/><line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Study Operations</h3>
        <p>Active studies stay uninterrupted during migration waves. Cutover is managed, scoped, and reversible — not a single high-risk switchover.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="persona-card">
        <div class="persona-icon">
          <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.07 4.93A10 10 0 1 0 4.93 19.07"/><path d="M19.07 4.93L12 12"/></svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Program Leadership</h3>
        <p>Clear migration unit status, controlled wave planning, and a defined engagement structure from scoping workshop through final cutover.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 7: How an Engagement Unfolds
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section" id="engagement">
    <div class="engagement-layout">
      <div class="engagement-content">
        <h2>How an engagement unfolds.</h2>

    <ol class="timeline">

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">1</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Scoping Workshop</h3>
          <p>Data volumes, study types, source systems, regulatory constraints.</p>
          <p class="phase-output"><strong>Output:</strong> a clear picture of what you're migrating, and when.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">2</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Mapping Exercise</h3>
          <p>Translate legacy model to target structure.</p>
          <p class="phase-output"><strong>Output:</strong> validated mapping spec and migration unit definitions.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">3</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Pilot Migration</h3>
          <p>Execute first wave end-to-end. Produce first real validation package. Resolve edge cases.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="phase">
        <div class="phase-number" aria-hidden="true">4</div>
        <div class="phase-content">
          <h3>Migration at Scale</h3>
          <p>Controlled waves with cutover management, lineage visibility, and audit-ready documentation throughout.</p>
        </div>
      </li>

    </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="engagement-image">
        <img
          src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/services/ipad-right.jpg`}
